From a8da0eb5fc49d49c1f85b5b6567d07652bf01cb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 09:42:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild view layer as Volt dark design system (7 screens)

Implements the VoltScreensHTML mockups as native SwiftUI, view layer only:

- Design tokens: asset-catalog named colors (voltBackground/Surface/
  SurfaceDeep/Accent/Danger/TextPrimary + coin brand accents), Spacing/
  Radius grid, Typography scale (SF Pro labels, SF Mono for all digits)
- Shared components: CoinRow, ChangePill, PrimaryButton, SparklineView,
  LiveDot, SectionCard, FilterPill, SidePill, CoinBadge, skeleton shimmer
- Watchlist: search bar, sparkline coin rows, change pills, LIVE dot,
  skeleton loading (no spinners)
- Trade ticket: full-width Buy/Sell toggle, USD amount entry with live
  coin-quantity estimate, slippage pills, 52pt confirm, last-fill recap
- Asset detail: hero price, teal/red candlestick chart with long-press
  OHLC crosshair, range pills, volume pane
- Portfolio: hero total value, unrealised P&L, position rows, allocation
  bar with legend
- History: All/Buys/Sells + coin/range filters, B/S pills, P&L per fill,
  outlined Export CSV footer
- Analytics: 2x2 stat cards, teal equity curve, daily P&L bars
- Settings: grouped cards for profile/data source/slippage/scenario/risk
  warnings, destructive Reset Portfolio with confirmation
- Root: 5-tab custom bar (Watchlist/Chart/Portfolio/Trade/Analytics),
  Settings via gear sheet, History via Portfolio toolbar; legacy tab
  restoration values remapped

ViewModels only gained view-bound state (watchlist sparkline buffer,
trade-ticket slippage mirror/setter via existing preferences path, stored
fill result); no trade engine, persistence, or fetching changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
